diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 9464d9a..21bf7b6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -109,20 +109,38 @@ from 0.17 to 0.50. P@5 cannot exceed 0.20 when a query has one relevant chunk.
 
 A chunk is returned only if it passes the gates in `config.py`:
 
-| Setting | Meaning |
-|---|---|
-| `MAX_DISTANCE` | dense distance gate for open questions |
-| `BM25_SOLO_MIN_SCORE` (default 12) | a chunk found *only* by BM25 needs this score; chunks dense also returned need any positive score. Raw BM25 scores of out-of-scope questions reach 11.4 and overlap real hits (6-12), so a single low floor cannot separate them |
-| `RERANK_MIN_SCORE` (default off) | cross-encoder cutoff; not applied to "browse" requests (question-type filter) |
-
-`python eval_sweep.py` caches embeddings and re-ranker scores, sweeps the three gates, and
-prints the best MRR whose false-retrieval rate is <= `--max-false-rate` (default 0.17),
-plus the `.env` lines to use. The gold set is both tuning and report set, so quote the swept
-numbers only after adding new, unseen queries.
-
-`python eval_retrieval.py --misses` writes `eval/results/misses.md`: for every missed query,
-whether the gold phrase is in any chunk at all, where the gold chunk ranks, and what was
-retrieved instead.
+| Setting | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `MAX_DISTANCE` | 0.55 | dense distance gate for open questions |
+| `BM25_SOLO_MIN_SCORE` | 6 | a chunk found *only* by BM25 needs this score when the re-ranker runs; chunks dense also returned need any positive score |
+| `BM25_SOLO_MIN_SCORE_NO_RERANK` | 12 | stricter bar when the re-ranker is off or unavailable (with 6 and no re-ranker, 6 of 12 out-of-scope queries retrieved something) |
+| `RERANK_MIN_SCORE` | -8.6 | cross-encoder cutoff, tuned for `Xenova/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2` only; off if `RERANK_MODEL` is overridden. Not applied to "browse" requests (question-type filter) |
+
+The defaults are the pick of `eval_sweep.py` on the 78-query gold set. In that sweep the top
+settings were within about 0.03 MRR of each other, i.e. a plateau, and the gold set is both
+tuning and report set, so treat the numbers as optimistic. Re-run the sweep whenever the models
+or the gold set change.
+
+`python eval_sweep.py` caches embeddings and re-ranker scores, sweeps the gates, and prints the
+best MRR whose false-retrieval rate is <= `--max-false-rate` (default 0.17), plus the `.env`
+lines.
+
+### Held-out check
+
+`eval/heldout_set.jsonl` has 34 answerable and 8 out-of-scope queries that were *not* used for
+tuning (no shared queries or answer phrases with the gold set; enforced by a test). Report these
+numbers, not the sweep numbers:
+
+```bash
+python eval_retrieval.py --translate --gold eval/heldout_set.jsonl --out eval/results/heldout
+```
+
+### Diagnosing misses
+
+`python eval_retrieval.py --misses` writes `eval/results/misses.md`: counts of misses by cause
+(`gold` = answer phrase in no chunk, `ranking` = relevant chunk in the top-20 but not top-5,
+`gate` = not in the top-20), the re-ranker/BM25/dense scores of the gold chunk, and every
+out-of-scope query that still retrieved something.
 
 ### "Important questions"
 
